The tests in this directory are specialized NVMeoF hosts which must be
run against an NVMeoF controller.  The address of the controller is
specified via FreeBSD Test Suite configuration variables which can be
passed to kyua(1) or set in configuration variable as described in
tests(7).

A sample ctl.conf file is included in this directory which can be used
with ctld(8) to provide a suitable test controller.  To use this file,
start ctld(8) by running the following as root:

# ctld -f /usr/tests/sys/cam/ctl/nvmft/ctl.conf

Then set the following configuration variables:

test_suites.FreeBSD.nvmft.address = "127.0.0.1"
test_suites.FreeBSD.nvmft.port = "4420"
test_suites.FreeBSD.nvmft.nqn = "nqn.1994-09.org.freebsd:test"

In addition, the following optional configuration variables may also
be set (Note that the variable names all require a prefix of
'test_suites.FreeBSD.'):

Name			Type	Default		Description
nvmft.transport		string	"tcp"		Transport type
nvmft.flow_control	bool	false		Request SQ flow_control
nvmft.cntlid		string	"dynamic"	Controller ID, can be
						"dynamic", "static", or
						a numeric value
nvmft.header_digests	bool	false		Request TCP header digests
nvmft.data_digests	bool	false		Request TCP data digests
